{"skill":{"slug":"summarize-pro","displayName":"Summarize Pro"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1771753198757,"changelog":"v1.0.0 — 20-feature AI summarizer with TL;DR, ELI5, meeting notes, multi-language, gamification","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":17743,"sha256":"59ab8eaf917e519126718acb54aeda9f4c53b98b9f8f68ee6207fd601ec52af3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2103,"sha256":"be780ff81adbcc49c5ad94497e4526b64903f9a737ac34d59ef93ee23485a9d3","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789078240937,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"8f8b6ff90d69b940c96d4f05cd4e93c43b355c3710854ad027760301e5c89f33","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/8f8b6ff90d69b940c96d4f05cd4e93c43b355c3710854ad027760301e5c89f33","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: summarize-pro\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills bundle 'summarize-pro' appears benign. The `SKILL.md` explicitly states that all processing happens locally, with 'NO external API calls, NO network requests, NO data sent to any server.' All file operations (read/write) are strictly confined to the `~/.openclaw/summarize-pro/` directory for managing settings, history, and saved summaries. The only shell command instructed is `mkdir -p` for initial setup, which is benign. There are no indications of prompt injection attempts, data exfiltration, malicious execution, or persistence mechanisms. The requested `read` and `write` permissions are justified by the skill's stated purpose of local data management.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779166168973},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":39,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":6,"checkedAt":1789078240937},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a local summarization skill whose file storage is disclosed and scoped to its own OpenClaw directory.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The requested read/write tools match the disclosed local JSON settings, history, saved summaries, and template storage under ~/.openclaw/summarize-pro/.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The package contains a single Markdown skill file, no executable scripts, no dependencies, and no remote payload retrieval.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Activation phrases include broad terms such as \"summary\" and \"compare,\" which could invoke the skill in ordinary conversation, but the resulting behavior remains limited to summarization and local management commands.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill creates persistent local files and automatically logs summary metadata, but this is disclosed, limited to the skill directory, capped for history, and not implemented through startup hooks, services, or background tasks.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The described capabilities are summarization formats, translations, comparisons, history, saved summaries, stats, and templates, all consistent with the stated summarizer purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with local history, stats, saved summaries, and templates being stored under ~/.openclaw/summarize-pro/. Avoid using it for highly sensitive documents unless you plan to manage or delete that local history.","findings":"[RA2] expected: The first-run directory, settings, and history files are real, but they are disclosed local state for preferences and usage tracking rather than hidden system persistence.\n[SQP-1] expected: The activation list is broad for a summarizer, so accidental invocation is possible, but the artifact does not pair this with network access, credential use, or arbitrary file access.\n[SQP-2] expected: Automatic history logging is present; the artifact discloses storage locations and keeps history to the last 100 entries, though users should be aware sensitive topics may remain locally.\n[RA2] expected: Custom templates are saved locally only when the user creates them; the artifact shows no cron jobs, startup scripts, or unauthorized background persistence.\n[EA3] expected: Multi-language summaries are within the stated summarization purpose, not unrelated scope expansion.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789078240937}}}}}